# Study Studio — environment reference
#
# READ THIS FIRST
# Study Studio is a statically exported Next.js app (`output: "export"`) bundled
# into a Tauri desktop shell. There is no Node server at runtime.
#
# Consequence: only variables prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` are inlined into the
# client bundle. A bare variable such as `OLLAMA_URL` is replaced with
# `undefined` in the shipped app, so the code falls back to its hard-coded
# default. `.env` is therefore NOT a configuration surface for the desktop app.
#
# What IS a configuration surface:
#   * Runtime settings (provider, base URL, model, API keys) -> the Settings
#     page in the app. Persisted by src/lib/ai-runtime/providerStore.ts.
#   * Node/Jest context only -> the variables below, which tests set directly.
#
# See docs/AI_RUNTIME.md for the provider contract.

# --- Local runtime -----------------------------------------------------------
# LM Studio is the primary local runtime. In LM Studio open the Developer tab,
# start the server (default port 1234), then choose a model in Study Studio's
# model dropdown. The app loads it into memory for you — no need to preload it
# in the LM Studio UI.
#
# Ollama (default port 11434) is supported when installed.
#
# Read by src/lib/ollama.ts. Inert in the desktop build unless injected via the
# `env` key in next.config.mjs — the app's Settings page is the real override.
OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434

# --- Retry policy ------------------------------------------------------------
# Base backoff between retries of a failed generation call, in milliseconds.
# Read by src/lib/generation.ts. Set to 0 in tests to avoid real sleeping.
#
# The doubled "STUDIO_STUDIO" is not a typo in this file — the code reads that
# exact name. It is kept as-is so existing setups do not silently lose it.
STUDIO_STUDIO_RETRY_BACKOFF_MS=1500

# --- Remote providers (optional) --------------------------------------------
# Do NOT set these here. Anything in this file ships inside the app bundle and
# is readable by anyone who has it. Enter remote keys in the Settings page,
# which stores them locally instead of compiling them in.
#
# Read by src/lib/ai-runtime/providers/openaiCompatible.ts.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Test-only ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Set to 1 to enable the skipped end-to-end podcast test.
# E2E_PODCAST=1
